---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CRYSTAL_BALL_PASS_DESCRIPTION, CRYSTAL_BALL_PASS_TRAIL } from '../lib/crystal-ball-pass';
import { AFTERLIGHT_ROUTES } from '../lib/crystal-ball-pass-v2';
import '../styles/crystal-ball-pass-landing.css';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CreativeWorkSeries',
  '@id': 'https://pointcast.xyz/crystal-ball-pass#world',
  name: 'Crystal Ball Pass',
  description: 'An expanding PointCast forest world with two playable browser expeditions, Codex Micro field notes, generated sound, and optional camp magic.',
  url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/crystal-ball-pass',
  image: 'https://pointcast.xyz/images/crystal-ball-pass/og.png',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PointCast × Codex', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz' },
  hasPart: [
    { '@type': 'VideoGame', name: 'The Original Passage', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/crystal-ball-pass/play' },
    { '@type': 'VideoGame', name: 'Afterlight', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/crystal-ball-pass/v2' },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Crystal Ball Pass — A growing forest adventure"
  description="The trailhead for Crystal Ball Pass: play the original five-minute expedition, enter V2 Afterlight, and follow new field notes from Codex Micro."
  image="/images/crystal-ball-pass/og.png"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  alternates={[{ type: 'application/json', href: '/crystal-ball-pass.json', title: 'Crystal Ball Pass world manifest' }]}
>
  <main class="trailhead">
    <header class="trailhead__bar">
      <a href="/" aria-label="PointCast home"><b>✦</b> POINTCAST</a>
      <nav aria-label="Crystal Ball Pass navigation">
        <a href="#passages">PASSAGES</a>
        <a href="#field-notes">FIELD NOTES</a>
        <a href="/reviews/crystal-ball-pass">REVIEW</a>
        <a href="/crystal-ball-pass.json">JSON ↗</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section class="trailhead__hero">
      <div class="trailhead__hero-image" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/images/crystal-ball-pass/og.png" alt="" width="1536" height="1024" />
        <div class="trailhead__mist"></div>
        <div class="trailhead__grain"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="trailhead__hero-copy">
        <span>THE TRAILHEAD · PACIFIC NORTHWEST, APPROXIMATELY</span>
        <h1>CRYSTAL<br />BALL PASS</h1>
        <p>One small forest. Two complete passages. A pocket computer with too many opinions about weather.</p>
        <div class="trailhead__hero-actions">
          <a class="trailhead__button trailhead__button--light" href="/crystal-ball-pass/v2">ENTER V2: AFTERLIGHT <b>→</b></a>
          <a class="trailhead__button" href="/crystal-ball-pass/play">PLAY THE ORIGINAL <b>↗</b></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="trailhead__hero-index">
        <span>WORLD 01</span>
        <span>2 PASSAGES</span>
        <span>~10 MIN TOTAL</span>
        <span>NO ACCOUNT</span>
      </div>
      <a class="trailhead__down" href="#passages"><span>SCROLL INTO THE FOREST</span><b>↓</b></a>
    </section>

    <section class="trailhead__passages" id="passages">
      <div class="trailhead__section-head">
        <span>CHOOSE A PASSAGE</span>
        <p>Both trails are complete, browser-local, and built to finish before the tea goes cold.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trailhead__passage-grid">
        <article class="trailhead__passage trailhead__passage--original">
          <div class="trailhead__passage-number">01</div>
          <div class="trailhead__passage-copy">
            <span>THE ORIGINAL · DAY TRAIL</span>
            <h2>FORTY-TWO MILES OF<br />WET SOCKS AND WONDER.</h2>
            <p>Seven Oregon Trail-sized decisions through foxfire, improbable mushrooms, a rude barometer, and one patient light.</p>
            <dl>
              <div><dt>DURATION</dt><dd>5 MIN</dd></div>
              <div><dt>FORKS</dt><dd>7 × 2</dd></div>
              <div><dt>SOUND</dt><dd>GENERATED</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a href="/crystal-ball-pass/play">BEGIN THE ORIGINAL PASSAGE →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="trailhead__tiny-map" aria-label="Seven original trail stops">
            {CRYSTAL_BALL_PASS_TRAIL.map((scene, index) => (
              <div><i>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</i><span>{scene.place}</span><b>{scene.weather.split(' · ')[0]}</b></div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="trailhead__passage trailhead__passage--afterlight">
          <div class="trailhead__afterglow" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><b>◇</b></div>
          <div class="trailhead__passage-number">02</div>
          <div class="trailhead__passage-copy">
            <span>V2 · NIGHT SIGNAL</span>
            <h2>THE PASS WAS ONLY<br />THE BEGINNING.</h2>
            <p>Choose a lost broadcast after dark. Each route is a distinct three-stop journey with its own writing, signal tones, kit, and ending.</p>
            <div class="trailhead__route-list">
              {AFTERLIGHT_ROUTES.map((route) => (
                <span style={`--route:${route.hue}`}><i></i>{route.name}<small>{route.callSign}</small></span>
              ))}
            </div>
            <a href="/crystal-ball-pass/v2">FOLLOW AN AFTERLIGHT SIGNAL →</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trailhead__notes" id="field-notes">
      <div class="trailhead__notes-title">
        <span>CODEX MICRO / FIELD NOTES</span>
        <h2>THE FOREST IS NOW<br />A PUBLISHING SYSTEM.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="trailhead__notes-grid">
        <article>
          <span>NOTE 001 · SCALE</span>
          <p>“A five-minute game can still contain weather, consequence, a joke worth keeping, and a place you remember tomorrow.”</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>NOTE 002 · V2</span>
          <p>“More is not a larger map. More is three routes that genuinely sound, read, and end differently.”</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>NOTE 003 · CAMP MAGIC</span>
          <p>“Spotify and Hue remain optional official handoffs. The forest receives no account, playback, bridge, or light data.”</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <aside class="trailhead__dispatch">
        <div>
          <span>AVAILABLE FOR CONTENT / V2</span>
          <h3>FIELD REPORTS, ROUTE NOTES, SOUND LETTERS, AND THE NEXT STRANGE CABIN.</h3>
        </div>
        <p>Crystal Ball Pass is built as a world, not a one-off page. New passages can arrive as playable routes; smaller observations can live here as Codex Micro dispatches without diluting the games.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="trailhead__review">
      <div class="trailhead__rating"><strong>4.6</strong><span>/ 5<br />POINTCAST<br />REVIEW LAB</span></div>
      <blockquote>“A small, complete forest story with excellent atmosphere, funny writing, and just enough survival math to make every pretty route feel dangerous.”</blockquote>
      <a href="/reviews/crystal-ball-pass">READ THE FULL REVIEW ↗</a>
    </section>

    <footer class="trailhead__footer">
      <a href="/">POINTCAST</a>
      <span>CRYSTAL BALL PASS · WORLD EDITION 1.1 · 2026</span>
      <div><a href="/crystal-ball-pass/play">V1</a><a href="/crystal-ball-pass/v2">V2</a><a href="/b/0550">BLOCK 0550</a></div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
